# The Work and Personal sweeps' filters (sd:5096, sd:5097): what each realm's Run sweep reads on this machine.
#
# Copy this file to <config>/project-dashboard/sweep.conf and edit it
# (<config> is $SYSTEM_TOOLS_CONFIG, default ~/.config/system); the values below
# are examples. Queries, projects and organisations are your own, so the real
# file stays outside the checkout.
#
# Pipe-separated, one setting per line:
#
#   <realm>|<key>|<value>
#
# <realm> is work or personal. The Google accounts are not here: the sweeps read
# google.accounts.work.email and google.accounts.personal.email from the pack's
# config.json. A key left out is a source the sweep skips, and its brief says so;
# mail, and work's followups, are required.
#
#   mail         a Gmail search; the sweep adds after:<last run>
#   skip-drives  shared Drives the sweep leaves alone, comma-separated
#   notion       work only: the teamspace or pages to search
#   jira         work only: a JQL clause, such as project in (...)
#   github       work only: a search qualifier, such as org:<name>
#   followups    work only: the registered checkout work followups belong to,
#                one a realms.conf work glob matches, so they show under Work

# Personal: leave out the HOA aliases and Drives; the HOA sweep reads them.
personal|mail|in:inbox -to:change-me@example.test -category:promotions
personal|skip-drives|Change-me HOA Drive, Change-me Committee Drive

work|mail|in:inbox -category:promotions -from:change-me@example.test
work|notion|change-me teamspace
work|jira|project in (CHANGEME)
work|github|org:change-me
work|followups|~/repos/example-work/change-me
